## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                  ← starts the server (and ORM connection, if any)
├── app.ts                   ← composition root — wires everything manually (no DI container)
├── config/env.ts            ← the only file that reads process.env
├── middlewares/              ← error handling, validation glue
├── shared/                   ← database/cache clients used by more than one module
├── core/
│   ├── entities/             ← domain entities — pure business objects, no framework dependencies
│   ├── ports/                ← abstract interfaces (repository contracts) the core depends on
│   └── use-cases/<module>/   ← application-specific business rules — one class per operation
└── adapters/<module>/
    ├── controllers/          ← Express req/res handlers
    ├── routes/               ← Express Router factory (injected with the wired controller)
    ├── presenters/           ← maps domain entities → views/DTOs
    ├── dto/                  ← input shapes / validation schemas
    └── repositories/         ← concrete implementations of core ports (Prisma, TypeORM, Mongoose, in-memory)
```

Dependency rule: `core/` knows nothing about `adapters/`. The composition root (`app.ts`) wires adapters into core ports by hand.

